      "problem": "Solve the equation ${3}^{y}=81.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $81$ as ${3}^{4}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{y} & =81 \\\\ {3}^{y} & ={3}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(3)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{y} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=4.$",
